## SQ-SV-01
@group A
@commands End: `/execute in minecraft:the_end run tp` an armor stand to 300016 100 300016 (ST-232); then a pearl onto Myalite at a spire viaduct
@pass The tp takes milliseconds, no "ticks behind", no region file at the target; the viaduct warp still works
@fails
@reviewed 2026-11-16
# the region at 300016 / 300016 is r.585.585 in DIM1; the viaduct pearl half needs a located spire viaduct (look)
> execute in minecraft:the_end run forceload add 0 0
> execute in minecraft:the_end run summon minecraft:armor_stand 0 100 0 {Tags:["sv01"],NoGravity:1b}
> execute in minecraft:the_end run tp @e[tag=sv01,limit=1] 300016 100 300016
> cdevtest tickwarp 40
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=40 60
> execute in minecraft:the_end run kill @e[tag=sv01]
> execute in minecraft:the_end run forceload remove 0 0
reject Can't keep up|ticks behind
shell test -z "$(ls */DIM1/region/r.585.585.mca 2>/dev/null)"
look the tp reply came at once (row log timestamps); the Myalite spire viaduct pearl warp is not in the batch: a located viaduct and a thrown pearl, record it as not run unless done by hand
